<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n91146" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πτερο-φόρᾱς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, ὀ</span>, a name of certain
		sacred officers in Egypt, so called from the hawk's <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>wing worn</i> on their heads, nom. pl. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-φόραι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>OGI</u>
					56.4
				</span></i>
			 (Canopus, <span class="entity">iii B.C.</span>), <i><span class="en">
				90.7
			</span></i> (Rosetta, <span class="entity">ii B.C.</span>): also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-φόροι</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>; cf. sq. <i><span class="en">
				111
			</span></i>, and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πτεραφόρος</span>.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> dat. sg. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-φόρᾳ χιλιάρχῳ</span>, perh. name of a
			military rank, or 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πτεροφόρος</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				11
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Men.
				<u>Pk.</u>
				104
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
			
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πτεροφόροι</span>
			.</div>
